# General rule first: later patterns override earlier ones in gitattributes,
# so the specific exemption below has to come last to win.
* text=auto

# The raw sources are evidence, not text to be tidied.
#
# Git's default is to normalise line endings on checkout, which rewrites bytes
# per platform. That would break every sha256 in data/raw/checksums.json the
# moment someone cloned this on Linux or macOS - the integrity check would fail
# and the failure would look like tampering rather than a git setting.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so the committed bytes are the
# bytes everyone gets.
data/raw/** -text
